@TITLE Zork I
@AUTHOR Adapted from Infocom (1980)
@START west_house
@DESC_TEXT The Great Underground Empire awaits.

@ROOM west_house
@DESC
You are standing in an open
field west of a white house,
with a boarded front door.
There is a small mailbox here.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Open the mailbox" -> mailbox_read
@CHOICE "Go behind the house" -> behind_house
@CHOICE "Enter the forest" -> forest

@ROOM mailbox_read
@DESC
Opening the small mailbox
reveals a leaflet. It reads:

"WELCOME TO ZORK! Your goal
is to collect treasures and
deposit them in the trophy
case inside the white house.
Straying recklessly is unwise."
@ENDDESC
@SCORE +5
@CHOICE "Close the mailbox" -> west_house

@ROOM behind_house
@DESC
You are behind the white house.
A path leads into the forest
to the east. In one corner of
the house there is a small
window which is slightly ajar.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Open the window" -> kitchen
@CHOICE "Go to the forest" -> forest
@CHOICE "Go back" -> west_house

@ROOM forest
@DESC
This is a forest, with trees
in all directions. To the east
a path leads deeper into
shadow. Songbirds chirp in the
branches overhead. All paths
seem to lead back to the house.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Go back to the house" -> west_house

@ROOM kitchen
@DESC
You are in the kitchen of the
white house. A table seems to
have been used recently for
the preparation of food.
@IF !has_lunch
A brown paper lunch sack
sits on the table.
@ENDIF
A passage leads west and a
dark staircase leads down.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Take the lunch sack" -> lunch_taken @NEED !has_lunch
@CHOICE "Go west" -> living_room
@CHOICE "Go upstairs" -> attic
@CHOICE "Go down the stairs" -> cellar @NEED has_light
@CHOICE "Descend into darkness" -> dark_stairs @NEED !has_light

@ROOM lunch_taken
@DESC
You take the brown paper sack
from the table. Inside is a
reasonably appetizing sandwich,
a clove of garlic, and a glass
of water. A practical lunch.
@ENDDESC
@ON_ENTER @SET has_lunch
@CHOICE "Continue" -> kitchen

@ROOM living_room
@DESC
You are in the living room.
There is a doorway to the east,
a wooden door with strange
gothic lettering to the west,
which appears to be nailed shut.
@IF !got_sword
An elvish sword of great
antiquity hangs above the
trophy case.
@ENDIF
@IF !got_lantern
A battery-powered brass
lantern is on the mantelpiece.
@ENDIF
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Take the sword" -> sword_taken @NEED !got_sword @SET got_sword
@CHOICE "Take the lantern" -> lantern_taken @NEED !got_lantern @SET got_lantern
@CHOICE "Go east" -> kitchen
@CHOICE "Open the trophy case" -> trophy_case

@ROOM sword_taken
@DESC
Taken. The sword is an elvish
blade of incredible sharpness.
Faint runes shimmer along
its length. It practically
hums with ancient purpose.
@ENDDESC
@ON_ENTER @GIVE sword "Elvish Sword" "A finely crafted blade. Faint runes shimmer along its length."
@ON_ENTER @SET has_sword
@CHOICE "Continue" -> living_room

@ROOM lantern_taken
@DESC
Taken. The brass lantern flares
to life as you lift it from
the mantle. Its beam is strong
and steady. This should light
even the deepest cellar.
@ENDDESC
@ON_ENTER @GIVE lantern "Brass Lantern" "A sturdy battery-powered lamp. Its beam is strong and steady."
@ON_ENTER @SET has_light
@CHOICE "Continue" -> living_room

@ROOM attic
@DESC
This is the attic. The only
exit is a stairway leading
down. A large coil of rope is
lying in the corner. On a
table is a nasty-looking knife.
@ENDDESC
@ITEM knife "Nasty Knife" "A rusty knife. Not much of a weapon, but unsettling."
@CHOICE "Go downstairs" -> kitchen

@ROOM cellar
@DESC
You are in a damp cellar with
a narrow passageway leading
north, and a crawlway to the
south. The stairs go up to the
kitchen.
@IF has_sword
Your sword glows with a faint
blue light.
@ENDIF
@ENDDESC
@ON_ENTER @SET visited_cellar
@CHOICE "Go north" -> troll_room
@CHOICE "Go south" -> coal_mine
@CHOICE "Go upstairs" -> kitchen

@ROOM dark_stairs
@DESC
You have moved into a dark
place. It is pitch black. You
are likely to be eaten by a
grue.

Oh no! A grue!
@ENDDESC
@GAMEOVER "You were eaten by a grue. An unspeakably horrible fate."

@ROOM troll_room
@DESC
A nasty-looking troll, holding
a great bloody axe, blocks all
passages out of the room. He
looks thoroughly displeased to
see you.
@IF has_sword
Your sword glows more brightly!
The troll eyes it nervously.
@ENDIF
@IF troll_cleared
The troll lies defeated in the
corner. The passages are clear.
@ENDIF
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Attack with sword" -> troll_victory @NEED has_sword
@CHOICE "Offer the lunch" -> troll_fed @NEED has_lunch
@CHOICE "Try to sneak past" -> troll_fail @NEED !troll_cleared
@CHOICE "Go north" -> maze_entrance @NEED troll_cleared

@ROOM troll_victory
@DESC
A brilliant swordfight ensues!
The troll is disarmed and flees
down a passage with a howl of
rage. Somehow you feel this
was the correct approach.
@ENDDESC
@SCORE +20
@ON_ENTER @SET troll_cleared
@CHOICE "Go north" -> maze_entrance

@ROOM troll_fed
@DESC
You extend the lunch sack. The
troll sniffs, snatches it, and
devours the sandwich in one
enormous bite. He belches
contentedly and wanders off.
Not the most heroic solution.
@ENDDESC
@SCORE +15
@ON_ENTER @SET troll_cleared
@CHOICE "Go north" -> maze_entrance

@ROOM troll_fail
@DESC
The troll flings you back with
contemptuous ease. You land in
an undignified heap. He resumes
blocking the passage, looking
even more annoyed than before.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Try something else" -> troll_room

@ROOM maze_entrance
@DESC
You are in a maze of twisty
little passages, all alike.
Identical corridors stretch in
every direction. A sign on the
wall reads: "Straying recklessly
IS unwise."
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Go left" -> maze_middle
@CHOICE "Go right" -> maze_entrance
@CHOICE "Go straight" -> maze_exit
@CHOICE "Go back south" -> troll_room

@ROOM maze_middle
@DESC
You are in a maze of twisty
little passages, all alike.
Wait, was that the same sign?
No, this one reads: "All the
same, all different." How
philosophically unhelpful.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Go left" -> maze_entrance
@CHOICE "Go right" -> maze_exit
@CHOICE "Go straight" -> maze_middle

@ROOM maze_exit
@DESC
You emerge from the maze into
a wider passage heading east.
Behind you, the twisty passages
seem to shift and rearrange.
There is no going back that way.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Go east" -> dam_lobby

@ROOM dam_lobby
@DESC
You are in a large cavern which
serves as the entrance to Flood
Control Dam #3. Passages lead
north, south, and east. A sign
reads: "FCD#3 - Scenic Vista"
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Go north" -> dam_top
@CHOICE "Go south" -> loud_room
@CHOICE "Go east" -> mine_shaft
@CHOICE "Go back west" -> maze_entrance

@ROOM dam_top
@DESC
You are standing on the top of
Flood Control Dam #3, which
was quite a technological
achievement in its day. A huge
sluice gate stands before you.
A control bolt protrudes from
the gate mechanism.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Turn the bolt" -> dam_opened @NEED wrench
@CHOICE "Search around" -> dam_search @NEED !has_wrench
@CHOICE "Go south" -> dam_lobby

@ROOM dam_search
@DESC
Searching along the railing,
you find a large wrench lodged
behind a control panel. Someone
left this here centuries ago.
How thoughtful of them.
@ENDDESC
@ON_ENTER @GIVE wrench "Wrench" "A large, heavy wrench. Perfect for turning bolts."
@ON_ENTER @SET has_wrench
@CHOICE "Go back to the gate" -> dam_top

@ROOM dam_opened
@DESC
With great effort, you turn
the bolt with the wrench. The
sluice gates groan and slowly
open. Water thunders through!
The reservoir begins to drain,
revealing a passage below.
@ENDDESC
@SCORE +15
@ON_ENTER @SET dam_open
@CHOICE "Go down to reservoir" -> reservoir @USE wrench

@ROOM reservoir
@DESC
You are on the muddy bottom of
what was once a vast reservoir.
Fish flop helplessly among the
puddles. The smell is appalling.
Something metallic glints in
the muck nearby.
@ENDDESC
@SCORE +5
@ITEM platinum_bar "Platinum Bar" "A heavy bar of pure platinum, stamped with imperial marks."
@CHOICE "Go back up" -> dam_lobby

@ROOM loud_room
@DESC
This is a large room with a
ceiling which is too high to
see. An incredible roar of
water fills the room, making
it impossible to hear or even
think clearly.
@IF echo_done
The room is now eerily quiet.
The echo has been broken.
@ENDIF
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Shout ECHO" -> loud_silenced @NEED !echo_done
@CHOICE "Go north" -> dam_lobby
@CHOICE "Go south" -> temple

@ROOM loud_silenced
@DESC
"ECHO!" you shout. The room
thunders back: "Echo...echo..."
Then silence falls like a
curtain. The roar of water
fades to nothing. On a stone
pedestal you can now see a
jeweled egg!
@ENDDESC
@SCORE +15
@ON_ENTER @SET echo_done
@ITEM jeweled_egg "Jeweled Egg" "An intricately decorated egg encrusted with precious gems."
@CHOICE "Go back" -> loud_room

@ROOM temple
@DESC
This is the interior of a
large temple. On the altar is
a beautiful gold chalice,
intricately engraved with
scenes of ancient worship.
Passages lead north and east.
@ENDDESC
@ITEM chalice "Gold Chalice" "A heavy gold chalice, beautifully engraved."
@CHOICE "Go north" -> loud_room
@CHOICE "Go east" -> cellar

@ROOM mine_shaft
@DESC
You are in a narrow mine shaft
which runs roughly north-south.
Timbers brace the walls at
intervals. The air is thick
with coal dust. The floor is
littered with old mining tools.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Go north" -> coal_mine
@CHOICE "Go south" -> thief_lair
@CHOICE "Go west" -> dam_lobby

@ROOM coal_mine
@DESC
You are in a coal mine. The
walls are streaked with black
veins of coal. Among the dark
rubble, something catches the
light of your lantern with
an unmistakable brilliance.
@ENDDESC
@ITEM diamond "Huge Diamond" "An enormous diamond. It sparkles with incredible fire."
@CHOICE "Go south" -> mine_shaft
@CHOICE "Go north" -> cellar

@ROOM thief_lair
@DESC
This appears to be the lair of
a large thief. Strewn about
are fine furnishings evidently
stolen from some mansion. The
thief himself eyes you from
across the room, a stiletto
in his hand.
@IF has_sword
Your elvish sword blazes with
blue light at the danger!
@ENDIF
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Fight with sword" -> thief_defeated @NEED has_sword
@CHOICE "Try to negotiate" -> thief_robs
@CHOICE "Retreat" -> mine_shaft

@ROOM thief_defeated
@DESC
Your elvish blade flashes in
the lamplight! The thief
parries once, twice, but on
the third stroke you disarm
him completely. He flees into
the darkness, leaving behind
an ornate gold coffin.
@ENDDESC
@SCORE +25
@ON_ENTER @SET thief_dead
@ITEM gold_coffin "Gold Coffin" "An ornate gold coffin inlaid with lapis lazuli."
@CHOICE "Go north" -> mine_shaft

@ROOM thief_robs
@DESC
You attempt to reason with the
thief. He listens with apparent
interest, then deftly relieves
you of all your possessions
and vanishes into the shadows.
You really should have expected
that.
@ENDDESC
@GAMEOVER "The thief robbed you blind. A sword might have helped."

@ROOM trophy_case
@DESC
You stand before the glass
trophy case. It is a handsome
case, clearly designed to hold
three great treasures. A plaque
reads: "For Adventurer's Use."
@IF placed_egg
The jeweled egg glitters
inside the case.
@ENDIF
@IF placed_coffin
The gold coffin gleams darkly.
@ENDIF
@IF placed_all
All three treasures rest within!
The case radiates with light.
@ENDIF
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Place jeweled egg" -> deposit_egg @NEED jeweled_egg
@CHOICE "Continue depositing" -> gate_coffin @NEED placed_egg
@CHOICE "Go to living room" -> living_room

@ROOM deposit_egg
@DESC
You carefully place the jeweled
egg in the trophy case. It
catches the light and throws
tiny rainbows across the room.
One treasure down.
@ENDDESC
@SCORE +10
@ON_ENTER @SET placed_egg
@CHOICE "Continue" -> gate_coffin @USE jeweled_egg

@ROOM gate_coffin
@DESC
The trophy case holds the
jeweled egg. Two spaces remain
for the gold coffin and the
enormous diamond.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Place gold coffin" -> deposit_coffin @NEED gold_coffin
@CHOICE "Continue depositing" -> gate_diamond @NEED placed_coffin
@CHOICE "Go find more treasure" -> living_room

@ROOM deposit_coffin
@DESC
The gold coffin fits neatly
into the case. Lapis lazuli
inlays shimmer in the lamplight.
Your collection is growing.
Two down, one to go.
@ENDDESC
@SCORE +10
@ON_ENTER @SET placed_coffin
@CHOICE "Continue" -> gate_diamond @USE gold_coffin

@ROOM gate_diamond
@DESC
Egg and coffin gleam in the
trophy case. One space remains
for the final treasure: the
enormous diamond.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Place the diamond" -> deposit_diamond @NEED diamond
@CHOICE "Go find the diamond" -> living_room

@ROOM deposit_diamond
@DESC
You set the enormous diamond
in the case. It catches every
photon of light in the room
and hurls it back tenfold.
All three treasures blaze with
an ancient power. The case hums.
@ENDDESC
@SCORE +10
@ON_ENTER @SET placed_all
@CHOICE "Claim your reward" -> victory @USE diamond

@ROOM victory
@DESC
Congratulations, Adventurer!
Having placed all treasures in
the trophy case, you are now
the rightful master of the
Great Underground Empire.

Your wisdom and bravery are
the stuff of legend. ZORK has
been conquered!
@ENDDESC
@SCORE +50
@WIN "Master of the Great Underground Empire! Score: {score}"
